# HR-011: Offboarding Checklist

**Document ID:** HR-011
**Title:** Offboarding Checklist and Procedure
**Version:** 1.0
**Effective Date:** January 17, 2026
**Owner:** HR & People Department (Rachel Williams, CHRO)

---

## 1. Policy Statement and Purpose

The MedSync Health Offboarding Checklist and Procedure ensures a consistent, compliant, and respectful process for the separation of employment, whether voluntary or involuntary. A structured offboarding process is critical for maintaining **data security**, protecting intellectual property, ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements (e.g., **HIPAA Compliance** certified March 2020 [1]), and facilitating a smooth transition of responsibilities.

This policy is governed by the principles outlined in the **MedSync Health General Policies (HR-001)** [2].

## 2. Scope and Eligibility

This procedure applies to all **1,200 employees** [3] of MedSync Health across all global offices (Boston, London, Berlin, Singapore) and all employment levels (Individual Contributor, Manager, Director, and VP).

**Exceptions:** Specific contractual obligations for C-Level executives (Average Compensation: AED 1,838,250 [3]) may supersede parts of this policy, as determined by the General Counsel (Robert Foster) and the CHRO (Rachel Williams).

## 3. General Offboarding Procedure

### 3.1. Notice and Communication
*   **Voluntary Separation:** Employees are required to provide a minimum of two (2) weeks' written notice. Managers and Directors are strongly encouraged to provide three (3) weeks, and VPs four (4) weeks.
*   **Involuntary Separation:** Handled confidentially by the HR & People Department (Headcount: 55 [3]) and Legal team (part of Finance & Legal, Headcount: 65 [3]).
*   **Exit Interview:** A mandatory exit interview will be conducted by HR for all voluntary separations to understand the reasons for departure and to help manage the **Voluntary Attrition Rate (12.5% in FY 2024)** [3].

### 3.2. Final Pay and Benefits
*   Final pay, including accrued but unused vacation time, will be processed on the next scheduled payroll date following the last day of employment.
*   Information regarding COBRA and continuation of benefits will be provided by the Finance team (Michael Rodriguez, CFO).
*   All outstanding expense reports must be submitted and approved prior to the last day of employment. Given the company's current **Burn Rate of AED 1,874,250 per month** [3], timely financial closure is essential.

## 4. Offboarding Checklist (Standard Procedure)

The following checklist is divided by responsible party and must be completed for all separating employees.

| Task Category | Responsible Party | Action Item | Deadline |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Manager** | Direct Manager | Complete knowledge transfer plan and assign a successor. | Last Day |
| | | Review and approve all outstanding expense reports. | Last Day |
| | | Conduct a final 1:1 meeting and collect all team-specific assets (keys, specialized equipment). | Last Day |
| **HR & People** | HR Partner | Process final payroll and benefits termination. | 1 Day Post-Exit |
| | | Conduct mandatory exit interview and document findings. | Last Day |
| | | Confirm return of all company property (signed off by IT). | 3 Days Post-Exit |
| **IT & Security** | IT Operations | Revoke all system access (SSO, VPN, SaaS tools). | End of Last Day |
| | | Collect and audit all company-issued devices (laptop, phone, tablet). | Last Day |
| | | Archive employee's email and network drive data. | 5 Days Post-Exit |
| **Finance** | Finance Team | Finalize expense reports and process final payment. | Payroll Date |
| | | Process final stock option/equity paperwork. | 7 Days Post-Exit |

## 5. Level-Based Variations

The complexity of the offboarding process scales with the employee's level, reflecting differences in access, financial responsibility, and communication requirements.

| Level | Average Compensation (AED) [3] | Key Offboarding Variation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Individual Contributor (IC)** | 294,000 | Standard checklist. Focus on asset return and knowledge transfer within the team. |
| **Manager** | 441,000 | Mandatory review of direct report performance files and succession planning for the team. |
| **Director** | 661,500 | Mandatory Legal/Compliance review of all documents created/managed. **Mandatory 90-day non-solicitation period review.** |
| **VP** | 1,102,500 | **Executive Communication Protocol:** CHRO and CEO (Dr. Sarah Chen) must approve all internal/external communications. **Board Access Revocation:** Immediate revocation of all board/executive committee access. |

